+# Wire Format
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use CBOR (Concise Binary Object Representation) as the serialization format for internal messages. The recorded rationale is that CBOR preserves type information better across protocol versions, which keeps messages compatible as schemas and types evolve; this prioritises schema flexibility and forward/backward compatibility over raw serialization compactness.
